 has length $a=8$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{8}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{81}{4}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295043 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dea75317-4676-5892-9874-67ea7ff4cdf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dea75317-4676-5892-9874-67ea7ff4cdf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293799} :answer-field/id #uuid "b698fac5-48ad-5a4b-97a3-0c37682df74c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294584}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "087f317c-361a-5e32-80c0-0140a69715d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-279126" :question/problem "![](images/41/410a33acd13bc05e65a8f11defb9828a68bf5b80826305adefe2d008afa245c4.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{11}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\righ